            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of syncope.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of a woman, who had previously undergone tubal sterilization, and later experienced two episodes of orthostatic hypotension during menstruation, as a result of an ectopic pregnancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
